# Data & Database

## Static vs MongoDB

Do **not** fetch static content from MongoDB. Keep in code, constants, JSON, or config:

- Navbar, footer, hero, about, contact info, company stats, static banners/services

Store in MongoDB only dynamic / admin-managed content:

- Products, categories, blogs, testimonials, projects, quotes, form submissions, CMS sections

## Query optimization

- Fetch only required fields (projections). No full-document dumps when partial data suffices.
- Paginate large lists. Index searchable fields.
- Avoid duplicate queries; reuse fetched data in the same flow.
- Minimize round-trips; never query for convenience alone.
